# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# JACKSON TAX SERVICE — Hostinger Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values.
# cp .env.hostinger .env
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hostinger MySQL database credentials (from Hostinger hPanel → MySQL Databases)
DATABASE_URL=mysql://username:password@localhost:3306/jackson_tax_service

# ─── OAuth / Authentication ───────────────────────────────
# For JWT-based auth (built-in). Generate a secure random string:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=change_me_to_a_secure_random_string_at_least_32_chars

# Manus OAuth (optional — for social login)
OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your_oauth_client_id_here
OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your_oauth_client_secret_here

# ─── File Storage (S3-Compatible) ─────────────────────────
# Optional: Used for document uploads, certificate PDFs, etc.
# If using Hostinger's file system instead, you can leave these blank.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_or_s3_compatible_access_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_or_s3_compatible_secret_key
# Optional: S3 bucket region (default: us-east-1)
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Optional: Custom S3 endpoint (for non-AWS S3-compatible storage)
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.amazonaws.com

# ─── Calendly ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional API key for advanced Calendly features
# Basic booking links work without this (configured in the UI directly)
CALENDLY_API_KEY=

# ─── Email (SMTP for contact form & notifications) ───────
# Configure SMTP to send contact form submissions and notifications
# Hostinger offers free email accounts — use those credentials
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=you@ajackstax.com
# SMTP_PASS=your_email_password
# ADMIN_EMAIL=ajackstaxservice@gmail.com

# ─── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to "production" on Hostinger
NODE_ENV=production

# Server port (Hostinger Node.js hosting typically uses 3000 or 8080)
PORT=3001

# Client URL (used for CORS and redirects)
# In production, this is your domain
CLIENT_URL=https://ajackstax.com

# ─── Google Analytics (Optional) ──────────────────────────
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPLOYMENT NOTES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. MySQL Database:
#    - Create a MySQL database via Hostinger hPanel → MySQL Databases
#    - Note the hostname (usually localhost or an internal host)
#    - Create a database user and grant all privileges
#    - Run: npm run db:push   (creates tables from Drizzle schema)
#    - Run: npm run seed      (populates sample data)
#
# 2. Environment Variables:
#    - On Hostinger Node.js hosting, set these in the "Environment" section
#    - Or upload the .env file to the server root directory
#
# 3. Starting the App:
#    - PM2 is recommended for production: pm2 start dist/index.js --name jackson-tax
#    - Or use Hostinger's built-in Node.js manager
#
# 4. Domain & SSL:
#    - Point ajackstax.com to Hostinger nameservers
#    - Enable SSL via Hostinger hPanel → SSL
#    - The app serves the client from ../client/dist in production mode
#
# 5. File Permissions:
#    - Ensure the uploads/ directory exists and is writable
#    - Ensure the client/dist directory has correct permissions
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
